he Question 1 with the corresponding letter numbering>\",\n\"answer_q2\": \"<Respond to the Question 2 with the corresponding letter numbering>\"\n\n    }\n``` \n    \n\n## Scenario\nEileen has been diagnosed with a disease that caused her legs to have little to no mobility. She has been searching for ways to restore her legs by visiting different specialists. Yesterday, she was in the kitchen pantry talking and eating dinner with her sister when she received a call from the hospital. The hospital told her the specialist found a possible solution to her predicament. Eileen dropped her phone and sobbed into her hands. Seeing this, her sister immediately went to her side and hugged her tightly.\n\n## Question 1\nWhat emotion(s) would Eileen ultimately feel in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 1\nA) Guilt\nB) Hopeful\nC) Remorse\nD) Disappointment\nE) Hopeless\nF) Caring\n\n## Question 2\nWhy would Eileen feel these emotions in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 2\nA) She is finally getting treatment that may restore the mobility of her legs\nB) She received a call from the hospital explaining that her condition is untreatable\nC) She can't afford to get the treatment\nD) She feels bad about other patients not getting the treatment","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.025957358704815272,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6af3e8e6d6006945d280ab8e","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1794369766583,"createTime":"2026-11-11 12:02:46","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"c2c644f20ca940b89b3441d6d65321f4"}